<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Aurora → S3 → Redshift Pipeline — glue-etl Component (BB-1917)</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
/* ============ THEME (Blueprint) ============ */
:root {
  --font-body: 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, sans-serif;
  --font-mono: 'IBM Plex Mono', 'SF Mono', Consolas, monospace;

  /* Light-first blueprint */
  --bg: #f5f7fa;
  --surface: #ffffff;
  --surface2: #eef2f7;
  --surface-elevated: #ffffff;
  --border: rgba(30, 58, 95, 0.12);
  --border-bright: rgba(30, 58, 95, 0.22);
  --text: #0f1e31;
  --text-dim: #54657d;
  --accent: #1e3a5f;           /* navy */
  --accent-dim: rgba(30, 58, 95, 0.08);
  --gold: #b07d0d;             /* gold */
  --gold-dim: rgba(176, 125, 13, 0.1);
  --teal: #0f766e;
  --teal-dim: rgba(15, 118, 110, 0.09);
  --green: #16633e;
  --green-dim: rgba(22, 99, 62, 0.09);
  --crimson: #9f1239;
  --crimson-dim: rgba(159, 18, 57, 0.09);
  --slate: #475569;
  --slate-dim: rgba(71, 85, 105, 0.09);
}

@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    --bg: #0b121c;
    --surface: #121b28;
    --surface2: #1a2434;
    --surface-elevated: #1a2434;
    --border: rgba(125, 179, 229, 0.12);
    --border-bright: rgba(125, 179, 229, 0.26);
    --text: #e1e8f0;
    --text-dim: #8fa3bf;
    --accent: #7db3e5;
    --accent-dim: rgba(125, 179, 229, 0.13);
    --gold: #d4a73a;
    --gold-dim: rgba(212, 167, 58, 0.14);
    --teal: #5eead4;
    --teal-dim: rgba(94, 234, 212, 0.12);
    --green: #4ade80;
    --green-dim: rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.12);
    --crimson: #fda4af;
    --crimson-dim: rgba(253, 164, 175, 0.12);
    --slate: #94a3b8;
    --slate-dim: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12);
  }
}

/* ============ RESET + BASE ============ */
* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
  background: var(--bg);
  background-image:
    linear-gradient(var(--border) 1px, transparent 1px),
    linear-gradient(90deg, var(--border) 1px, transparent 1px);
  background-size: 48px 48px;
  background-position: -1px -1px;
  color: var(--text);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  padding: 40px;
  min-height: 100vh;
  line-height: 1.55;
}

/* ============ ANIMATION ============ */
@keyframes fadeUp { from {opacity:0; transform:translateY(10px);} to {opacity:1;transform:translateY(0);} }
.sec-head, .ve-card, .risk-row, .pipeline-step { animation: fadeUp 0.35s ease-out both; animation-delay: calc(var(--i,0) * 0.04s); }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { *,*::before,*::after { animation-duration:0.01ms !important; animation-delay:0ms !important; transition-duration:0.01ms !important; } }

/* ============ LAYOUT ============ */
.wrap { max-width: 1400px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 180px 1fr; gap: 0 40px; }
.main { min-width: 0; }

/* ============ TOC (Sticky sidebar) ============ */
.toc { position: sticky; top: 24px; align-self: start; padding: 14px 0; grid-row: 1 / -1; max-height: calc(100dvh - 48px); overflow-y: auto; }
.toc::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 3px; }
.toc::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb { background: var(--surface-elevated); border-radius: 2px; }
.toc-title { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-dim); padding: 0 0 10px; margin-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.toc a { display: block; font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-dim); text-decoration: none; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 4px; border-left: 2px solid transparent; transition: all 0.15s; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 1px; font-family: var(--font-mono); }
.toc a:hover { color: var(--text); background: var(--surface2); }
.toc a.active { color: var(--accent); border-left-color: var(--gold); background: var(--surface); }

/* ============ TYPOGRAPHY ============ */
h1 { font-size: 40px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -1.2px; margin-bottom: 6px; text-wrap: balance; }
h1 .h1-sub { display: block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 400; color: var(--gold); letter-spacing: 1px; margin-top: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; }
.subtitle { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 32px; max-width: 720px; }

.sec-head { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2.5px; color: var(--accent); padding: 24px 0 12px; margin-top: 28px; margin-bottom: 14px; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.sec-head::before { content: attr(data-num); font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--gold); letter-spacing: 0; }
.sec-head::after { content: ''; flex: 1; height: 1px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--gold-dim), transparent); }

h3 { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; margin: 18px 0 10px; color: var(--text); }

/* ============ CARD (ve-card) ============ */
.ve-card { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; position: relative; }
.ve-card--hero { background: var(--surface-elevated); box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(15, 30, 49, 0.05); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--border) 40%, var(--gold) 60%); padding: 28px 32px; }
.ve-card--recessed { background: var(--surface2); box-shadow: inset 0 1px 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04); }
.ve-card--accent { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); }
.ve-card--gold { border-left: 3px solid var(--gold); }
.ve-card--teal { border-left: 3px solid var(--teal); }
.ve-card--green { border-left: 3px solid var(--green); }
.ve-card--crimson { border-left: 3px solid var(--crimson); }

.ve-card__label { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.8px; margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
.ve-card__label::before { content: ''; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: currentColor; }
.ve-card__label.c-accent { color: var(--accent); }
.ve-card__label.c-gold { color: var(--gold); }
.ve-card__label.c-teal { color: var(--teal); }
.ve-card__label.c-green { color: var(--green); }
.ve-card__label.c-crimson { color: var(--crimson); }
.ve-card__label.c-slate { color: var(--slate); }

.ve-card p { margin-bottom: 10px; color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 13.5px; }
.ve-card p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

/* ============ HERO STATS ============ */
.hero-stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(140px, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin-top: 18px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px dashed var(--border-bright); }
.hero-stat { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
.hero-stat__num { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 28px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: -0.5px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.hero-stat__num .unit { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-dim); font-weight: 400; margin-left: 2px; }
.hero-stat__label { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.2px; color: var(--text-dim); }

/* ============ GRID LAYOUTS ============ */
.grid-2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
.grid-3 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
.grid-auto { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 16px; }

/* ============ CODE ============ */
code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; background: var(--gold-dim); color: var(--gold); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 3px; }
.code-block { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.55; background: var(--surface2); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px 16px; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; color: var(--text); }
.code-block .kw { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
.code-block .str { color: var(--green); }
.code-block .cm { color: var(--text-dim); font-style: italic; }
.code-block .nm { color: var(--gold); }

/* ============ TABLE ============ */
.tbl-wrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--surface); }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; }
thead { background: var(--surface2); position: sticky; top: 0; }
th { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.2px; color: var(--text-dim); text-align: left; padding: 11px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); white-space: nowrap; }
td { padding: 11px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); vertical-align: top; color: var(--text); }
tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
tbody tr:nth-child(even) { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface2) 40%, var(--surface) 60%); }
tbody tr:hover { background: var(--accent-dim); }
td.num { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; text-align: right; }
td code, th code { font-size: 11px; }

/* Status pills */
.pill { display: inline-block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.8px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 10px; }
.pill--ok { background: var(--green-dim); color: var(--green); }
.pill--warn { background: var(--gold-dim); color: var(--gold); }
.pill--risk { background: var(--crimson-dim); color: var(--crimson); }
.pill--info { background: var(--accent-dim); color: var(--accent); }
.pill--muted { background: var(--slate-dim); color: var(--slate); }

/* ============ PIPELINE / TIMELINE ============ */
.pipeline { display: flex; gap: 0; align-items: stretch; overflow-x: auto; padding: 4px 0 12px; }
.pipeline-step { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; min-width: 180px; flex-shrink: 0; }
.pipeline-step__num { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--gold); margin-bottom: 4px; letter-spacing: 1.4px; text-transform: uppercase; }
.pipeline-step__name { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 6px; color: var(--accent); }
.pipeline-step__detail { font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--text-dim); line-height: 1.5; }
.pipeline-step__timing { display: inline-block; margin-top: 8px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; color: var(--text-dim); background: var(--surface2); padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 3px; }
.pipeline-arrow { display: flex; align-items: center; padding: 0 6px; color: var(--border-bright); font-size: 22px; flex-shrink: 0; }

/* ============ FLOW ARROW (vertical) ============ */
.flow-arrow { display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; gap: 10px; color: var(--text-dim); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; padding: 8px 0; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }
.flow-arrow svg { width: 16px; height: 16px; fill: none; stroke: var(--gold); stroke-width: 1.8; }

/* ============ CALLOUT ============ */
.callout { background: var(--surface2); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 3px solid var(--gold); border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; padding: 14px 18px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-dim); margin: 14px 0; }
.callout strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }

/* ============ LIST ============ */
.node-list { list-style: none; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.8; }
.node-list li { padding-left: 18px; position: relative; color: var(--text-dim); }
.node-list li::before { content: '›'; color: var(--gold); font-weight: 700; position: absolute; left: 4px; }
.node-list li strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }

/* ============ MERMAID WRAP ============ */
.mermaid-wrap { position: relative; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 32px; overflow: auto; cursor: grab; min-height: 640px; }
.mermaid-wrap--tall { min-height: 820px; }
.mermaid-wrap:active { cursor: grabbing; }
.mermaid-wrap .mermaid { width: 100%; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; }
/* Force Mermaid SVG to fill container width — default caps at intrinsic size, leaving dead space on wide viewports */
.mermaid-wrap .mermaid svg { width: 100% !important; max-width: 100% !important; height: auto !important; min-height: 560px; display: block; }
.mermaid-wrap--tall .mermaid svg { min-height: 760px; }
.mermaid .nodeLabel { color: var(--text) !important; font-family: var(--font-body) !important; font-size: 18px !important; font-weight: 500 !important; }
.mermaid .edgeLabel { color: var(--text-dim) !important; background-color: var(--bg) !important; font-family: var(--font-mono) !important; font-size: 14px !important; }
.mermaid .edgeLabel rect { fill: var(--bg) !important; }
.mermaid .node rect, .mermaid .node polygon, .mermaid .node circle { stroke-width: 2px; }
.mermaid .edge-pattern-solid { stroke-width: 1.8px; }
.mermaid .actor { stroke-width: 2px; }
.mermaid .messageText { font-family: var(--font-mono) !important; font-size: 15px !important; }
.mermaid .cluster rect { stroke-width: 1.6px; }
.mermaid .cluster text { font-size: 16px !important; font-weight: 600 !important; }

/* ============ KPI LABEL STRIP ============ */
.meta-strip { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 14px; margin: 4px 0 20px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-dim); }
.meta-strip span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
.meta-strip span::before { content: ''; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--gold); }

/* ============ SIDE BY SIDE ============ */
.side-by-side { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 12px; }

/* ============ RESPONSIVE ============ */
@media (max-width: 1000px) {
  body { padding-top: 0; padding-left: 20px; padding-right: 20px; }
  .wrap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding-top: 0; }
  .toc { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 200; max-height: none; display: flex; gap: 4px; align-items: center; overflow-x: auto; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; background: var(--bg); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 10px 0; margin: 0 -20px; padding-left: 20px; padding-right: 20px; grid-row: auto; }
  .toc::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
  .toc-title { display: none; }
  .toc a { white-space: nowrap; flex-shrink: 0; border-left: none; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; border-radius: 4px 4px 0 0; padding: 6px 10px; font-size: 10px; }
  .toc a.active { border-left: none; border-bottom-color: var(--gold); background: var(--surface); }
  .sec-head { scroll-margin-top: 52px; }
  .grid-2, .grid-3, .side-by-side { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  h1 { font-size: 30px; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="wrap">

<nav class="toc" id="toc">
  <div class="toc-title">Contents</div>
  <a href="#s1">01 / Overview</a>
  <a href="#s2">02 / Architecture</a>
  <a href="#s3">03 / Runtime Flow</a>
  <a href="#s4">04 / Terraform Layers</a>
  <a href="#s5">05 / COPY JOB Engine</a>
  <a href="#s6">06 / Preconditions</a>
  <a href="#s7">07 / Security</a>
  <a href="#s8">08 / Config Matrix</a>
  <a href="#s9">09 / Operator Playbook</a>
  <a href="#s10">10 / Risks &amp; Gotchas</a>
</nav>

<div class="main">

<h1>
  Aurora → S3 → Redshift
  <span class="h1-sub">glue-etl component · BB-1917 · verup project</span>
</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Daily snapshot pipeline for 22 Aurora MySQL tables into Redshift via Glue Spark ETL, S3 Parquet staging, and native Redshift COPY JOB. Ships AUTO ON by default so operators don't poll — Redshift reacts to S3 ObjectCreated events.</p>

<div class="meta-strip">
  <span>Terraform component <code>bs-exchange-infra/terraform/components/glue-etl</code></span>
  <span>Envs <code>dev-ex</code>, <code>stg-ex</code></span>
  <span>Daily 02:00 JST (17:00 UTC)</span>
  <span>AUTO ON</span>
</div>

<!-- ============ SECTION 1: OVERVIEW ============ -->
<div id="s1" class="sec-head" data-num="01">Overview</div>

<div class="ve-card ve-card--hero" style="--i:0">
  <div class="ve-card__label c-gold">System in one paragraph</div>
  <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text)">
    Every day at 02:00 JST, an AWS Glue scheduled trigger fires all 22 Glue Spark jobs in parallel.
    Each job reads one Aurora MySQL table via JDBC through a private-subnet ENI, writes Parquet
    (Snappy compressed, date-partitioned) to an SSE-KMS encrypted S3 bucket. Redshift's S3 Event
    Integration then watches the bucket and auto-fires each COPY JOB the moment a new file lands —
    loading into <code>"point"."glue_&lt;rds_table&gt;"</code> with double-quoted identifiers for
    reserved-keyword safety. Terraform owns the entire stack: networking, S3/KMS, Glue, IAM, and
    the Redshift load layer via a <code>NONATOMIC</code> stored procedure that makes per-table
    COPY JOB registration idempotent across applies.
  </p>
  <div class="hero-stats">
    <div class="hero-stat"><div class="hero-stat__num">22<span class="unit">tables</span></div><div class="hero-stat__label">Aurora → Redshift</div></div>
    <div class="hero-stat"><div class="hero-stat__num">30<span class="unit">resources</span></div><div class="hero-stat__label">Terraform inventory</div></div>
    <div class="hero-stat"><div class="hero-stat__num">3<span class="unit">preconditions</span></div><div class="hero-stat__label">apply-time gates</div></div>
    <div class="hero-stat"><div class="hero-stat__num">5–30<span class="unit">min</span></div><div class="hero-stat__label">full pipeline run</div></div>
    <div class="hero-stat"><div class="hero-stat__num">127<span class="unit">bytes</span></div><div class="hero-stat__label">Redshift id limit</div></div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:18px">
  <div class="ve-card ve-card--accent" style="--i:1">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-accent">Why this shape</div>
    <p>Zero-ETL was the first candidate but priced poorly for STG. Glue + S3 + native COPY JOB hits the same SLA (daily snapshot) using only native AWS primitives — no third-party ETL tooling.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="ve-card ve-card--gold" style="--i:2">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-gold">Per-table isolation</div>
    <p>One Glue Job + one COPY JOB per table. A failing table does not block the other 21; each has its own retry budget, manifest, and observability surface in CloudWatch and <code>sys_copy_job_details</code>.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="ve-card ve-card--teal" style="--i:3">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-teal">Idempotent apply</div>
    <p>A <code>NONATOMIC</code> PL/pgSQL procedure <code>upsert_copy_job()</code> wraps <code>COPY JOB DROP</code> + <code>CREATE</code> so re-applying Terraform with changed config always converges, with no stale state.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============ SECTION 2: ARCHITECTURE ============ -->
<div id="s2" class="sec-head" data-num="02">Architecture</div>

<div class="mermaid-wrap mermaid-wrap--tall" style="--i:0">
<pre class="mermaid">
graph TD
    Aurora["Aurora MySQL<br/>point · port 13306<br/>require_secure_transport"]

    subgraph GlueLayer ["AWS Glue &nbsp;·&nbsp; per table ×22"]
      direction LR
      GlueTrigger["Trigger<br/>cron 17:00 UTC<br/>= 02:00 JST"]
      GlueConn["Glue Connection<br/>ENI · private subnet<br/>JDBC+SSL"]
      GlueJob["Glue Job<br/>Spark 3.5.4 · Python 3.11<br/>G.1X × (2 dev / 3 stg)<br/>timeout 30m"]
    end

    subgraph Staging ["S3 Staging &nbsp;·&nbsp; SSE-KMS"]
      direction LR
      S3["s3://aurora-to-redshift-staging.*<br/>data/&lt;table&gt;/year=YYYY/month=MM/day=DD/<br/>TLS enforced · lifecycle 30d · versioned"]
      KMS[("KMS CMK<br/>alias/aurora-to-redshift-staging-&lt;env&gt;")]
    end

    subgraph RedshiftLayer ["Redshift Load"]
      direction LR
      S3Int["S3 Event Integration<br/>ObjectCreated → cluster"]
      CopyJob["COPY JOB<br/>&lt;table&gt;_copy_job · AUTO ON"]
      Target["point.glue_&lt;table&gt;<br/>DDL pre-exists"]
    end

    Aurora -->|"JDBC+SSL<br/>via SECRET_ID"| GlueConn
    GlueTrigger -->|"daily trigger"| GlueJob
    GlueConn --> GlueJob
    GlueJob -->|"Parquet · snappy"| S3
    S3 -.encrypted by.- KMS
    S3 -->|"ObjectCreated"| S3Int
    S3Int -->|"fires"| CopyJob
    CopyJob -->|"IAM_ROLE ·<br/>GetObject + Decrypt"| Target

    classDef src fill:#1e3a5f22,stroke:#1e3a5f,stroke-width:2px
    classDef glue fill:#b07d0d22,stroke:#b07d0d,stroke-width:1.8px
    classDef stage fill:#0f766e22,stroke:#0f766e,stroke-width:1.8px
    classDef rs fill:#16633e22,stroke:#16633e,stroke-width:1.8px
    class Aurora src
    class GlueConn,GlueJob,GlueTrigger glue
    class S3,KMS stage
    class S3Int,CopyJob,Target rs
</pre>
</div>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Legend</strong> — Navy: source of truth. Gold: extract layer (owns Aurora access).
  Teal: staging (owns encryption + retention). Green: load layer (reads S3 and writes Redshift).
  Dashed edges indicate cryptographic dependency; solid edges are data flow.
</div>

<!-- ============ SECTION 3: RUNTIME FLOW ============ -->
<div id="s3" class="sec-head" data-num="03">Runtime flow — 4 phases</div>

<div class="ve-card" style="--i:0">
  <div class="ve-card__label c-accent">Phase 1 · Trigger (~1s)</div>
  <p><code>aws_glue_trigger.scheduled</code> with cron <code>cron(0 17 * * ? *)</code> fires. A single trigger dispatches 22 jobs in parallel through a <code>dynamic "actions"</code> block iterating <code>var.tables</code>. Each job has <code>max_concurrent_runs = 1</code>, so the same table cannot overlap with itself, but all 22 race concurrently.</p>
</div>

<div class="flow-arrow" style="--i:1"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M8 2 v12 M4 10 l4 4 l4-4"/></svg>cron fires → Glue dispatcher</div>

<div class="ve-card ve-card--gold" style="--i:2">
  <div class="ve-card__label c-gold">Phase 2 · Extract · Aurora → S3 (~1–6 min per job)</div>
  <p><strong>Credential chain:</strong> Glue auto-fetches the Aurora secret via <code>SECRET_ID</code> stored in <code>aws_glue_connection.aurora</code> — the PySpark script never reads Secrets Manager directly. <code>useConnectionProperties=true</code> delegates credential resolution to the Glue Connection manager.</p>
  <p><strong>Network path:</strong> Glue ENI in private subnet → SG self-ref + egress to Aurora port 13306. JDBC enforces TLS via <code>JDBC_ENFORCE_SSL=true</code> to satisfy Aurora's <code>require_secure_transport</code> parameter.</p>
  <p><strong>Output:</strong> <code>s3://&lt;bucket&gt;/data/&lt;table&gt;/year=YYYY/month=MM/day=DD/part-*.parquet</code> with Snappy compression. SSE-KMS applied automatically by the Glue Security Configuration.</p>
</div>

<div class="flow-arrow" style="--i:3"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M8 2 v12 M4 10 l4 4 l4-4"/></svg>Parquet dropped on S3</div>

<div class="ve-card ve-card--teal" style="--i:4">
  <div class="ve-card__label c-teal">Phase 3 · Load · S3 → Redshift (~1–10 min per table)</div>
  <p><strong>AUTO ON path (default):</strong> S3 <code>ObjectCreated</code> event → S3 Event Integration (<code>aws_redshift_integration.s3_event</code>) → Redshift auto-fires the matching COPY JOB. No operator action. Typical lag 10–30s between Parquet land and load start.</p>
  <p><strong>AUTO OFF fallback:</strong> <code>CALL SYS_EXEC_COPY_JOB('user_copy_job')</code> via Redshift Data API. Redshift reads the stored job definition, lists the S3 prefix, skips files already in <code>sys_copy_job_details</code>, and loads the rest in parallel.</p>
  <p><strong>Target resolution:</strong> <code>COPY "point"."glue_user" FROM 's3://.../data/user/' IAM_ROLE 'arn:...' FORMAT AS PARQUET</code>. Double-quoted identifier survives an empty <code>redshift_table_prefix</code> without colliding with reserved keywords like <code>USER</code>.</p>
</div>

<div class="flow-arrow" style="--i:5"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M8 2 v12 M4 10 l4 4 l4-4"/></svg>rows committed to target</div>

<div class="ve-card ve-card--green" style="--i:6">
  <div class="ve-card__label c-green">Phase 4 · Terraform apply interaction</div>
  <p><strong>Install procedure once:</strong> <code>aws_redshiftdata_statement.install_upsert_proc</code> runs <code>CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE upsert_copy_job(...)</code>. Because the template content rarely changes, later applies are no-op on this resource.</p>
  <p><strong>Upsert per table:</strong> <code>aws_redshiftdata_statement.upsert_copy_job</code> (×22) calls the procedure, which drops the existing COPY JOB if present then creates a new one with the current rendered SQL + AUTO mode. Safe to re-run any number of times.</p>
</div>

<h3 style="margin-top:24px">Key timing table</h3>
<div class="tbl-wrap">
<table>
  <colgroup><col style="width:160px"><col><col style="width:140px"><col></colgroup>
  <thead><tr><th>Phase</th><th>Component</th><th>Duration</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Trigger</td><td>cron → Glue dispatcher</td><td class="num">&lt; 1s</td><td>All 22 dispatched concurrently</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Extract: connect</td><td>Glue ENI + secret fetch</td><td class="num">3–5s</td><td>Cold start may be slower</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Extract: read</td><td>Full Aurora table scan</td><td class="num">30s–5m</td><td>Depends on table size</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Extract: write</td><td>Parquet + multipart S3</td><td class="num">10–30s</td><td>Snappy compression</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Load: event</td><td>S3 ObjectCreated → COPY fire</td><td class="num">10–30s</td><td>AUTO ON only</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Load: COPY</td><td>S3 read → INSERT</td><td class="num">30s–10m</td><td>Parallel slice-level</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Total per table</strong></td><td>Aurora commit → Redshift commit</td><td class="num"><strong>5–30m</strong></td><td>Dominated by Glue runtime</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<!-- ============ SECTION 4: TERRAFORM LAYERS ============ -->
<div id="s4" class="sec-head" data-num="04">Terraform layers — 6 groups, 30 resources</div>

<div class="grid-auto">
  <div class="ve-card ve-card--accent" style="--i:0">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-accent">Networking · 6 resources</div>
    <ul class="node-list">
      <li><strong>aws_security_group.glue_conn</strong> — ENI SG, self-ref ingress+egress (Glue requirement), broad egress for service endpoints.</li>
      <li><strong>aws_security_group_rule.glue_to_aurora</strong> — egress on port 13306 to existing Aurora SG.</li>
      <li><strong>aws_security_group_rule.aurora_ingress_from_glue</strong> — reverse ingress rule attached to Aurora SG.</li>
      <li>Deterministic subnet selection via <code>sort(data.aws_subnets.private.ids)[0]</code> — no drift.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--teal" style="--i:1">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-teal">S3 + KMS Staging · 9 resources</div>
    <ul class="node-list">
      <li><strong>aws_kms_key.staging + alias</strong> — CMK with rotation; policy grants S3 service (SourceAccount-scoped), Glue role, Redshift role.</li>
      <li><strong>aws_s3_bucket.staging</strong> — versioning on, SSE-KMS enforced, public access blocked.</li>
      <li><strong>aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration.staging</strong> — two rules: <code>data/</code> expires in 30d; <code>_temporary/</code> in 1d. Empty-prefix rule would delete scripts → forbidden.</li>
      <li><strong>aws_s3_bucket_policy.staging</strong> — DenyInsecureTransport + DenyUnencryptedPut + 3 role-based allow statements.</li>
      <li><strong>aws_s3_object.glue_script</strong> — uploads <code>aurora_to_s3.py</code> with <code>filemd5</code> etag for change detection.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--gold" style="--i:2">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-gold">Glue · 4 resources</div>
    <ul class="node-list">
      <li><strong>aws_glue_security_configuration.staging</strong> — SSE-KMS for all job writes.</li>
      <li><strong>aws_glue_connection.aurora</strong> — JDBC + SSL + <code>SECRET_ID</code> reference.</li>
      <li><strong>aws_glue_job.table</strong> — <code>for_each</code> ×22, Glue 5.0, G.1X workers, per-table <code>--job-bookmark-option</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>aws_glue_trigger.scheduled</strong> — cron + dynamic <code>actions</code> dispatching all 22 jobs.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--crimson" style="--i:3">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-crimson">IAM · 5 resources</div>
    <ul class="node-list">
      <li><strong>aws_iam_role.glue_service</strong> — trust glue.amazonaws.com with SourceAccount condition.</li>
      <li><strong>glue_service_inline</strong> — GetSecretValue on Aurora secret, S3 RW on staging, KMS full on CMK.</li>
      <li><strong>aws_iam_role.redshift_copy</strong> — trust redshift.amazonaws.com, read-only S3 + Decrypt-only KMS.</li>
      <li>Managed policy <code>AWSGlueServiceRole</code> attached separately.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--green" style="--i:4">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-green">Redshift Load · 5 resources</div>
    <ul class="node-list">
      <li><strong>aws_redshift_cluster_iam_roles.copy</strong> — attaches COPY role to cluster so <code>IAM_ROLE '&lt;arn&gt;'</code> works.</li>
      <li><strong>install_upsert_proc</strong> — <code>aws_redshiftdata_statement</code> installing the procedure once per apply.</li>
      <li><strong>upsert_copy_job</strong> — <code>for_each</code> ×22, calls procedure per table with rendered COPY SQL.</li>
      <li><strong>aws_redshift_resource_policy.s3_event</strong> + <strong>aws_redshift_integration.s3_event</strong> — AUTO ON only; <code>count=0</code> when AUTO OFF.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--recessed" style="--i:5">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-slate">Data sources · 8 lookups</div>
    <ul class="node-list">
      <li><code>data.aws_vpc.vpc</code>, <code>data.aws_subnets.private</code>, <code>data.aws_subnet.glue_conn</code></li>
      <li><code>data.aws_security_group.mysql</code> — Aurora SG by tag:Name</li>
      <li><code>data.aws_rds_cluster.aurora</code> — endpoint for JDBC URL</li>
      <li><code>data.aws_secretsmanager_secret.aurora_user</code> — secret ARN + name</li>
      <li><code>data.aws_redshift_cluster.target</code> — namespace ARN for integration</li>
      <li><code>data.aws_caller_identity.current</code> — account ID for confused-deputy guards</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============ SECTION 5: COPY JOB Engine ============ -->
<div id="s5" class="sec-head" data-num="05">COPY JOB engine — the idempotent upsert</div>

<p style="color:var(--text-dim);font-size:14px;margin-bottom:14px;max-width:820px">
Redshift does not support <code>CREATE OR REPLACE COPY JOB</code>. A second <code>terraform apply</code>
with the same config would fail with "job already exists". The pipeline wraps native COPY JOB in a
<code>NONATOMIC</code> PL/pgSQL procedure that drops then recreates — turning non-idempotent DDL into
an idempotent Terraform operation. The native COPY JOB features (manifest, parallelism, AUTO ON) are
preserved entirely.
</p>

<div class="mermaid-wrap mermaid-wrap--tall" style="--i:0;margin-bottom:16px">
<pre class="mermaid">
sequenceDiagram
    participant TF as terraform apply
    participant RDA as Redshift Data API
    participant Cluster as Redshift Cluster
    participant SYS as sys_copy_job

    TF->>RDA: install_upsert_proc<br/>CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE
    RDA->>Cluster: execute
    Cluster-->>RDA: ok (idempotent)

    loop per table (×22)
      TF->>RDA: CALL upsert_copy_job(name, copy_sql, auto)
      RDA->>Cluster: execute
      Cluster->>SYS: SELECT COUNT(*) WHERE job_name=...
      alt exists
        Cluster->>SYS: COPY JOB DROP "name"
      end
      Cluster->>SYS: COPY &lt;target&gt; FROM ... JOB CREATE "name" AUTO ON
      Cluster-->>RDA: ok
    end

    RDA-->>TF: 22 statements FINISHED
</pre>
</div>

<div class="grid-2">
  <div class="ve-card ve-card--accent" style="--i:1">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-accent">sql/upsert_copy_job.sql.tftpl · NONATOMIC</div>
    <pre class="code-block"><span class="kw">CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE</span> upsert_copy_job(
  p_job_name <span class="nm">VARCHAR(128)</span>,
  p_copy_sql <span class="nm">VARCHAR(MAX)</span>,
  p_auto     <span class="nm">VARCHAR(3)</span>
) <span class="kw">NONATOMIC</span> <span class="kw">AS</span> $$
<span class="kw">DECLARE</span>
  v_exists <span class="nm">INT</span>;
<span class="kw">BEGIN</span>
  <span class="kw">SELECT COUNT</span>(*) <span class="kw">INTO</span> v_exists
    <span class="kw">FROM</span> sys_copy_job
   <span class="kw">WHERE TRIM</span>(job_name) = <span class="kw">TRIM</span>(p_job_name);

  <span class="kw">IF</span> v_exists &gt; 0 <span class="kw">THEN</span>
    <span class="kw">EXECUTE</span> <span class="str">'COPY JOB DROP '</span> || <span class="kw">quote_ident</span>(p_job_name);
  <span class="kw">END IF</span>;

  <span class="kw">EXECUTE</span> p_copy_sql || <span class="str">' JOB CREATE '</span>
    || <span class="kw">quote_ident</span>(p_job_name) || <span class="str">' AUTO '</span> || p_auto;
<span class="kw">END</span>;
$$ <span class="kw">LANGUAGE</span> plpgsql;</pre>
  </div>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--gold" style="--i:2">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-gold">redshift_copy_job.tf · format() call</div>
    <pre class="code-block">copy_sql = <span class="kw">format</span>(
  <span class="str">"COPY \"%s\".\"%s\" FROM 's3://%s/data/%s/' "</span>
  <span class="str">"IAM_ROLE '%s' FORMAT AS PARQUET"</span>,
  var.redshift_schema,              <span class="cm">// "point"</span>
  <span class="str">"${var.redshift_table_prefix}${each.key}"</span>,
                                    <span class="cm">// "glue_user"</span>
  aws_s3_bucket.staging[0].bucket,
  each.key,                         <span class="cm">// "user" (S3 path)</span>
  aws_iam_role.redshift_copy[0].arn,
)

<span class="cm">// Renders to:</span>
<span class="cm">// COPY "point"."glue_user"</span>
<span class="cm">//   FROM 's3://.../data/user/'</span>
<span class="cm">//   IAM_ROLE 'arn:...'</span>
<span class="cm">//   FORMAT AS PARQUET</span></pre>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Three identifiers, three different values</strong> — Redshift target is <code>point.glue_user</code>
  (schema + prefix), S3 path stays <code>data/user/</code> (raw RDS name so Glue output matches), COPY JOB
  name is <code>user_copy_job</code> (raw RDS name so <code>sys_copy_job</code> entries remain stable if the
  prefix ever changes).
</div>

<!-- ============ SECTION 6: PRECONDITIONS ============ -->
<div id="s6" class="sec-head" data-num="06">Lifecycle preconditions — 3 plan-time gates</div>

<p style="color:var(--text-dim);font-size:14px;margin-bottom:14px">Preconditions on
<code>aws_redshiftdata_statement.upsert_copy_job</code> evaluate at both <code>plan</code> and
<code>apply</code> time. They abort Terraform <strong>before</strong> any COPY JOB is touched, so a
misconfigured apply cannot leave half-registered jobs. Unlike <code>variable.validation</code>,
preconditions can reference multiple variables at once.</p>

<div class="grid-3">
  <div class="ve-card ve-card--teal" style="--i:0">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-teal">Precondition 1 · non-empty tables</div>
    <pre class="code-block"><span class="kw">condition</span> = <span class="kw">length</span>(var.tables) &gt; 0</pre>
    <p style="margin-top:10px">Triggers when <code>tables = []</code>. Without this, applying with an empty list would silently produce zero COPY JOB instances — operator sees "apply success" but nothing happened.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--gold" style="--i:1">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-gold">Precondition 2 · AUTO ON ↔ integration flag</div>
    <pre class="code-block"><span class="kw">condition</span> = !var.redshift_copy_job_auto
  || var.redshift_s3_event_integration_configured</pre>
    <p style="margin-top:10px">Logical implication "auto ON → flag ON". Fails if operator flips <code>auto=true</code> but forgets the ack flag. Prevents <code>InvalidIntegration</code> compile error inside Redshift.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--crimson" style="--i:2">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-crimson">Precondition 3 · identifier length ≤ 127</div>
    <pre class="code-block"><span class="kw">condition</span> = <span class="kw">alltrue</span>([
  <span class="kw">for</span> t <span class="kw">in</span> var.tables :
    <span class="kw">length</span>(<span class="str">"${var.redshift_table_prefix}${t}"</span>) &lt;= 127
])</pre>
    <p style="margin-top:10px">Redshift identifier limit is 127 bytes. Regex already caps prefix (32) + table (64) = 96 max, so this is belt-and-suspenders if regex is ever widened.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h3 style="margin-top:24px">Failure mode matrix</h3>
<div class="tbl-wrap">
<table>
  <colgroup><col style="width:36%"><col style="width:14%"><col></colgroup>
  <thead><tr><th>tfvars configuration</th><th>Precondition</th><th>Operator sees</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>tables = []</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--risk">fail #1</span></td><td>"Must have at least one table in var.tables..."</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>auto = true</code> + <code>configured = false</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--risk">fail #2</span></td><td>"redshift_copy_job_auto = true requires S3 Event Integration..."</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>auto = false</code> + <code>configured = anything</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">pass</span></td><td>AUTO OFF ignores the flag</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>auto = true</code> + <code>configured = true</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">pass</span></td><td>Normal AUTO ON apply</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Combined identifier &gt; 127 bytes (after regex widened)</td><td><span class="pill pill--risk">fail #3</span></td><td>"Combined length of redshift_table_prefix + each table..."</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>redshift_copy_job_enabled = false</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--muted">N/A</span></td><td>Resource has count=0, preconditions never evaluate</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<!-- ============ SECTION 7: SECURITY ============ -->
<div id="s7" class="sec-head" data-num="07">Security boundaries</div>

<div class="grid-2">
  <div class="ve-card ve-card--accent" style="--i:0">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-accent">Encryption</div>
    <ul class="node-list">
      <li><strong>S3 at rest:</strong> SSE-KMS with CMK <code>alias/aurora-to-redshift-staging-&lt;env&gt;</code>. Bucket key enabled.</li>
      <li><strong>S3 in transit:</strong> bucket policy <code>DenyInsecureTransport</code> rejects non-HTTPS.</li>
      <li><strong>S3 puts:</strong> bucket policy <code>DenyUnencryptedPut</code> rejects uploads missing <code>x-amz-server-side-encryption</code> header.</li>
      <li><strong>JDBC:</strong> <code>JDBC_ENFORCE_SSL=true</code> on Glue Connection matches Aurora's <code>require_secure_transport</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Redshift ↔ S3:</strong> cluster uses IAM role with KMS <code>Decrypt</code> only (read-path).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--gold" style="--i:1">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-gold">Confused-deputy guards</div>
    <ul class="node-list">
      <li><strong>IAM trust policies:</strong> both roles (glue_service, redshift_copy) require <code>aws:SourceAccount</code> = current account.</li>
      <li><strong>KMS policy:</strong> S3 service principal scoped to <code>aws:SourceAccount</code> — prevents cross-account role reuse.</li>
      <li><strong>S3 Event Integration:</strong> resource policy restricts <code>AuthorizeInboundIntegration</code> to the exact staging bucket ARN.</li>
      <li><strong>CMK to role binding:</strong> Redshift COPY role gets <code>Decrypt</code> only — never <code>Encrypt</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--teal" style="--i:2">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-teal">VPC boundary</div>
    <ul class="node-list">
      <li><strong>Glue ENI:</strong> lives in private subnet. Self-ref SG (Glue requirement) plus egress-all to reach service endpoints.</li>
      <li><strong>Aurora access:</strong> only port 13306 from Glue SG (narrow ingress). No CIDR-wide rule.</li>
      <li><strong>Redshift:</strong> not in the Glue VPC. Reads S3 over AWS internal network using its IAM role.</li>
      <li><strong>Single-AZ ENI:</strong> subnet pinned via <code>sort()[0]</code>. If AZ dies, re-apply to move.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--crimson" style="--i:3">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-crimson">Bucket policy principals (5 statements)</div>
    <ul class="node-list">
      <li><code>DenyInsecureTransport</code> — reject HTTP</li>
      <li><code>DenyUnencryptedPut</code> — reject plaintext PUT</li>
      <li><code>AllowGlueServiceRole</code> — RW for Glue write path</li>
      <li><code>AllowRedshiftCopyRole</code> — RO for Redshift read path</li>
      <li><code>AllowRedshiftEventIntegration</code> — <code>s3:GetBucketNotification</code> / <code>PutBucketNotification</code> scoped to integration ARN</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============ SECTION 8: CONFIG MATRIX ============ -->
<div id="s8" class="sec-head" data-num="08">Configuration matrix — DEV vs STG</div>

<p style="color:var(--text-dim);font-size:13px;margin-bottom:14px">All variables are explicitly declared in each tfvars — no reliance on <code>variables.tf</code> defaults. Only 4 operational values differ between environments.</p>

<div class="tbl-wrap">
<table>
  <colgroup><col style="width:32%"><col style="width:28%"><col style="width:28%"><col style="width:12%"></colgroup>
  <thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>DEV-EX</th><th>STG-EX</th><th>Delta</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td colspan="4" style="background:var(--surface2);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1.4px;color:var(--accent)">Core + network (identical)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>environment</code></td><td><code>dev-ex</code></td><td><code>stg-ex</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--info">env</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>region</code></td><td><code>ap-northeast-1</code></td><td><code>ap-northeast-1</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>vpc_name</code></td><td><code>point</code></td><td><code>point</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>mysql_sg_name</code></td><td><code>mysql-sg</code></td><td><code>mysql-sg</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>

    <tr><td colspan="4" style="background:var(--surface2);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1.4px;color:var(--accent)">Aurora source (identical)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>rds_aurora_name</code></td><td><code>point</code></td><td><code>point</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>aurora_port</code></td><td class="num">13306</td><td class="num">13306</td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>aurora_user_secret_name</code></td><td><code>point/aurora/viewer_user</code></td><td><code>point/aurora/viewer_user</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>

    <tr><td colspan="4" style="background:var(--surface2);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1.4px;color:var(--accent)">S3 staging (env-suffixed)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>staging_bucket_name</code></td><td><code>...bs-point-dev-ex</code></td><td><code>...bs-point-stg-ex</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--info">env suffix</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>staging_kms_alias</code></td><td><code>alias/...-dev-ex</code></td><td><code>alias/...-stg-ex</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--info">env suffix</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>staging_parquet_retention_days</code></td><td class="num">30</td><td class="num">30</td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>

    <tr><td colspan="4" style="background:var(--surface2);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1.4px;color:var(--accent)">Glue job config</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>glue_job_worker_type</code></td><td><code>G.1X</code></td><td><code>G.1X</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>glue_job_number_of_workers</code></td><td class="num">2</td><td class="num"><strong>3</strong></td><td><span class="pill pill--warn">+1</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>glue_job_timeout_minutes</code></td><td class="num">30</td><td class="num">30</td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>glue_job_max_retries</code></td><td class="num">1</td><td class="num">1</td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>trigger_schedule</code></td><td><code>cron(0 17 * * ? *)</code></td><td><code>cron(0 17 * * ? *)</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>

    <tr><td colspan="4" style="background:var(--surface2);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1.4px;color:var(--accent)">Redshift load + AUTO ON (identical)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>redshift_schema</code></td><td><code>point</code></td><td><code>point</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>redshift_table_prefix</code></td><td><code>glue_</code></td><td><code>glue_</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>redshift_copy_job_enabled</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>redshift_copy_job_auto</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">AUTO ON</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>redshift_s3_event_integration_configured</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>

    <tr><td colspan="4" style="background:var(--surface2);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1.4px;color:var(--accent)">Bookmark (identical)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>bookmark_mode_default</code></td><td><code>job-bookmark-enable</code></td><td><code>job-bookmark-enable</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">same</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>bookmark_mode_per_table</code></td><td><code>{}</code></td><td><code>{}</code></td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">empty</span></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<!-- ============ SECTION 9: OPERATOR PLAYBOOK ============ -->
<div id="s9" class="sec-head" data-num="09">Operator playbook</div>

<h3>Trigger a COPY JOB manually</h3>
<div class="side-by-side">
  <div class="ve-card ve-card--accent" style="--i:0">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-accent">Redshift query editor</div>
    <pre class="code-block"><span class="kw">CALL</span> SYS_EXEC_COPY_JOB(<span class="str">'user_copy_job'</span>);

<span class="cm">-- verify</span>
<span class="kw">SELECT</span> start_time, status, loaded_rows
  <span class="kw">FROM</span> sys_copy_job_details
 <span class="kw">WHERE</span> job_name = <span class="str">'user_copy_job'</span>
 <span class="kw">ORDER BY</span> start_time <span class="kw">DESC</span> <span class="kw">LIMIT</span> 5;</pre>
  </div>

  <div class="ve-card ve-card--gold" style="--i:1">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-gold">AWS CLI (Redshift Data API)</div>
    <pre class="code-block">aws redshift-data execute-statement \
  --cluster-identifier point-dev-ex \
  --database point \
  --db-user master \
  --sql <span class="str">"CALL SYS_EXEC_COPY_JOB('user_copy_job');"</span> \
  --region ap-northeast-1
<span class="cm"># returns Statement ID</span>

aws redshift-data describe-statement --id &lt;id&gt;
<span class="cm"># Status: FINISHED | FAILED | STARTED</span></pre>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>Flip AUTO ON from a clean slate</h3>
<div class="pipeline" style="--i:2">
  <div class="pipeline-step">
    <div class="pipeline-step__num">step 0</div>
    <div class="pipeline-step__name">Pre-checks</div>
    <div class="pipeline-step__detail">DDL exists · S3 has Parquet · KMS policy ok · no running COPY</div>
  </div>
  <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="pipeline-step">
    <div class="pipeline-step__num">step 1</div>
    <div class="pipeline-step__name">Set flags</div>
    <div class="pipeline-step__detail"><code>auto = true</code><br><code>configured = true</code></div>
  </div>
  <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="pipeline-step">
    <div class="pipeline-step__num">step 2</div>
    <div class="pipeline-step__name">terraform apply</div>
    <div class="pipeline-step__detail">resource policy → integration → 22 CALL upsert</div>
    <div class="pipeline-step__timing">≤ 30m</div>
  </div>
  <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="pipeline-step">
    <div class="pipeline-step__num">step 3</div>
    <div class="pipeline-step__name">Verify</div>
    <div class="pipeline-step__detail"><code>SELECT auto_on FROM sys_copy_job</code> → all 't'</div>
  </div>
  <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="pipeline-step">
    <div class="pipeline-step__num">step 4</div>
    <div class="pipeline-step__name">Smoke test</div>
    <div class="pipeline-step__detail">Drop Parquet to S3 · expect COPY row within 30s</div>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>Monitoring queries</h3>
<div class="grid-2">
  <div class="ve-card ve-card--teal" style="--i:3">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-teal">List all jobs</div>
    <pre class="code-block"><span class="kw">SELECT</span> job_name, auto_on, copy_command
  <span class="kw">FROM</span> sys_copy_job
 <span class="kw">ORDER BY</span> job_name;</pre>
  </div>
  <div class="ve-card ve-card--crimson" style="--i:4">
    <div class="ve-card__label c-crimson">Failed loads (24h)</div>
    <pre class="code-block"><span class="kw">SELECT</span> job_name, start_time, error_message, data_source
  <span class="kw">FROM</span> sys_copy_job_details
 <span class="kw">WHERE</span> status != <span class="str">'Completed'</span>
   <span class="kw">AND</span> start_time &gt; <span class="kw">DATEADD</span>(hour, -24, <span class="kw">GETDATE</span>())
 <span class="kw">ORDER BY</span> start_time <span class="kw">DESC</span>;</pre>
  </div>
</div>

<h3>Rollback to AUTO OFF</h3>
<div class="callout">
Edit tfvars: <code>redshift_copy_job_auto = false</code> and <code>redshift_s3_event_integration_configured = false</code>, then <code>terraform apply</code>. Terraform drops + recreates 22 COPY JOB with AUTO OFF, destroys the S3 Event Integration and its resource policy. Data in Redshift persists.
</div>

<!-- ============ SECTION 10: RISKS ============ -->
<div id="s10" class="sec-head" data-num="10">Known risks &amp; gotchas</div>

<div class="tbl-wrap">
<table>
  <colgroup><col style="width:22%"><col style="width:32%"><col style="width:32%"><col style="width:14%"></colgroup>
  <thead><tr><th>Risk</th><th>Symptom</th><th>Mitigation</th><th>Owner</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><strong>DDL not pre-created</strong></td><td>terraform apply succeeds; runtime COPY fails with <code>relation does not exist</code></td><td>App team (BB-1918) creates <code>point.glue_&lt;table&gt;</code> before flipping <code>copy_job_enabled</code>. Verify via <code>information_schema.tables</code>.</td><td><span class="pill pill--risk">HIGH</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Reserved-word table name</strong></td><td>With prefix empty, <code>user</code> would collide with keyword <code>USER</code></td><td>Double-quoted identifier in rendered COPY shields — verify <code>sys_copy_job.copy_command</code> shows <code>"point"."user"</code>.</td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">GUARDED</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Manifest reset on re-apply</strong></td><td>Each apply drops+creates COPY JOB, clearing <code>sys_copy_job_details</code> → next run may re-scan S3 prefix</td><td>Avoid Terraform apply between daily runs; apply only during maintenance windows.</td><td><span class="pill pill--warn">MED</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Remove table from var.tables</strong></td><td>Terraform destroys the state entry but doesn't run <code>COPY JOB DROP</code> in Redshift → zombie job</td><td>Operator runs manual <code>COPY JOB DROP "&lt;table&gt;_copy_job"</code> after removing from tfvars.</td><td><span class="pill pill--warn">MED</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Integration provisioning timeout</strong></td><td>30m timeout on <code>aws_redshift_integration.s3_event</code>. If fails, COPY JOB not registered</td><td>Retry <code>terraform apply</code>; resource policy persists so next attempt is faster. Check CloudTrail for KMS / policy errors.</td><td><span class="pill pill--warn">MED</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Job timeout vs _temporary/ TTL</strong></td><td>Glue temp files expire in 1 day. If job timeout &gt; 1440 min, temp files could expire mid-run</td><td>Variable validation caps <code>glue_job_timeout_minutes</code> at 1439.</td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">GUARDED</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Empty-prefix lifecycle rule</strong></td><td>Would delete <code>scripts/aurora_to_s3.py</code>, crashing all 22 jobs</td><td>Rules scoped to <code>data/</code> and <code>_temporary/</code> only. Never add empty-prefix rule.</td><td><span class="pill pill--ok">GUARDED</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Procedure manually dropped</strong></td><td>Terraform state doesn't track runtime state of procedure</td><td>Run <code>terraform taint aws_redshiftdata_statement.install_upsert_proc[0]</code> then apply.</td><td><span class="pill pill--warn">LOW</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Bookmark vs custom watermark conflict</strong></td><td>Glue bookmark and app-owned watermark (for UPDATE tables) diverge → dup/skipped rows</td><td>Use <code>bookmark_mode_per_table</code> to disable Glue bookmark for UPDATE-heavy tables. Currently empty; add per-table overrides if app team ships custom watermark.</td><td><span class="pill pill--warn">MED</span></td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Single-AZ Glue ENI</strong></td><td>If chosen AZ dies, Glue jobs fail until re-apply moves ENI</td><td>Re-apply Terraform. <code>sort()</code> is deterministic so picks the next available subnet only if topology changes.</td><td><span class="pill pill--warn">LOW</span></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<div class="callout" style="margin-top:24px">
<strong>Source of truth</strong> — this page is a synthesis of:
<code>bs-exchange-infra/terraform/components/glue-etl/</code> (component + tfvars),
<code>docs/sprints/sprint-21/1917/glue-alternative/redshift-copy-job-explained.md</code> (design deep-dive),
<code>docs/sprints/sprint-21/1917/glue-alternative/copy-job-operations.md</code> (ops runbook).
For exact deploy procedure, see <code>1917_DEPLOY_DEV-EX_GLUE.md</code> and <code>1917_DEPLOY_STG-EX_GLUE.md</code>.
</div>

</div><!-- /main -->
</div><!-- /wrap -->

